# Edge scheduler: bounded loops, a guarded while-task, and a periodic timer.
# The language now supports three iteration control-flow shapes:
#   REPEAT <N> TIMES ... END : fixed-count burst (with overflow guard)
#   WHILE <pin> [IS] HIGH|LOW ... END : conditional task (TOCTOU-guarded)
#   EVERY <N> MS ... END : cooperative periodic task (yields, never starves)
# Wiring: physical pin 18 (BCM 24) -> status LED output;
#         physical pin 24 (BCM 8)  -> door contact input.
# Run it: sentryc examples/scheduler.pi
LINK PIN 18 TO STATUS_LED AS OUTPUT
LINK PIN 24 TO DOOR_SENSOR AS INPUT

REPEAT 5 TIMES
    STATUS_LED HIGH
    DELAY 100 MS
    STATUS_LED LOW
    DELAY 100 MS
END

ATOMIC
    WHILE DOOR_SENSOR IS HIGH
        STATUS_LED HIGH
        LOG "Door open. Holding status LED lit."
    END
END

EVERY 1000 MS
    STATUS_LED LOW
    LOG "Scheduler heartbeat."
END